# InterWeave repository ignore policy
#
# Keep normative fixtures, test-data, example configuration, Cargo.lock, and
# architecture material visible to Git. Ignore only local state, credentials,
# generated outputs, and developer-machine artifacts.

# Rust / Cargo build outputs
/target/
**/target/
*.profraw
*.profdata
/coverage/
/lcov.info

# Cargo.lock is intentionally tracked for this application/workspace repository.
!Cargo.lock

# Android / Gradle generated state
.gradle/
**/.gradle/
**/build/
**/.cxx/
**/.externalNativeBuild/
**/captures/
**/local.properties
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.dex

# Native/JNI generated outputs
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll
*.dSYM/

# Local InterWeave runtime/profile state
/state/
/cache/
/run/
/tmp/
*.pid
*.sock
*.sock.lock
*.log
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal

# Local configuration and environment overrides
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
architecture/config/local.yaml
architecture/config/local.yml

# Credentials and private identity material. Test-only key material must use
# an explicitly documented fixture path/name rather than relying on these
# generic extensions.
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.secret
*.seed

# Per-developer coding-agent overrides — host machine details, personal
# scratch notes, never committed. `.claude/settings.json` IS committed:
# it is shared project configuration (the git-push gate, worktree base
# ref). Only the per-developer `*.local.json` overrides stay out.
CLAUDE.local.md
**/CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/settings.local.json

# Subagent worktrees. The harness creates these inside the repository and
# only auto-removes the ones an agent left unchanged, so a productive
# fan-out leaves real ones behind. Each holds a `.git` FILE, so a
# tree-wide `git add -A` would stage it as an embedded git repository and
# commit a broken gitlink.
.claude/worktrees/

# Editors / IDEs
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.example.json
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS metadata
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Generic temporary/generated files
*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# Normative/synthetic fixtures may intentionally exercise key container
# formats. These paths are reviewable test material, not local credentials.
!fixtures/**/*.pem
!fixtures/**/*.p12
!fixtures/**/*.pfx
!fixtures/**/*.jks
!fixtures/**/*.keystore
!fixtures/**/*.seed
!test-data/**/*.pem
!test-data/**/*.p12
!test-data/**/*.pfx
!test-data/**/*.jks
!test-data/**/*.keystore
!test-data/**/*.seed

# Python bytecode from ad-hoc tooling runs
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Spike build outputs. Spikes are outside the workspace, so each has its
# own target/ and lock file; neither is evidence.
spikes/**/target/
spikes/**/Cargo.lock
# ...EXCEPT where the resolved graph IS the evidence.
#
# A spike whose finding is version-sensitive cannot be reproduced from a
# floating requirement: `version = "0.56"` resolves a later 0.56.x, and
# the recorded result then describes a graph nobody can rebuild. SPIKE-002
# measures duplicate-cache ordering and timeout attribution, both of which
# are exactly the kind of behaviour a patch release may change, so its
# lock is committed and its direct requirements are pinned with `=`.
!spikes/spike-002/harness/Cargo.lock

# cargo-mutants writes its report tree into the working directory when
# `--output` is not given. It is build output, and a `git add -A` swept
# twenty-two of its files into a commit before this line existed.
mutants.out*/
